    "problem_statement": "LaTeX table output uses \\n instead of \\r\\n line endings\n\nI'm using PrettyTable to generate LaTeX tables for a document I'm working on, and I noticed that the line endings in the LaTeX output have changed.\n\nMinimal example:\n```python\nfrom prettytable import PrettyTable\n\ntable = PrettyTable()\ntable.field_names = [\"Field 1\", \"Field 2\", \"Field 3\"]\ntable.add_row([\"value 1\", \"value2\", \"value3\"])\ntable.add_row([\"value 4\", \"value5\", \"value6\"])\ntable.add_row([\"value 7\", \"value8\", \"value9\"])\n\nlatex_output = table.get_latex_string(format=True)\nprint(repr(latex_output))\n```\n\nExpected output (with \\r\\n line endings):\n```\n'\\\\begin{tabular}{|c|c|c|}\\r\\n\\\\hline\\r\\nField 1 & Field 2 & Field 3 \\\\\\\\\\r\\n\\\\hline\\r\\nvalue 1 & value2 & value3 \\\\\\\\\\r\\nvalue 4 & value5 & value6 \\\\\\\\\\r\\nvalue 7 & value8 & value9 \\\\\\\\\\r\\n\\\\hline\\r\\n\\\\end{tabular}'\n```\n\nActual output (with \\n line endings):\n```\n'\\\\begin{tabular}{|c|c|c|}\\n\\\\hline\\nField 1 & Field 2 & Field 3 \\\\\\\\\\n\\\\hline\\nvalue 1 & value2 & value3 \\\\\\\\\\nvalue 4 & value5 & value6 \\\\\\\\\\nvalue 7 & value8 & value9 \\\\\\\\\\n\\\\hline\\n\\\\end{tabular}'\n```\n\nThis breaks compatibility with my existing code that expects \\r\\n line endings. I also noticed that the alignment string generation seems to have changed, which affects tables with custom formatting options.\n\nI'm using this for a LaTeX document generation pipeline that has specific expectations about the format of the output. The change in line endings is causing issues with my document processing scripts."
